{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a massive cobbler-scaffold stitch task prompt (task #5492, branch `task/generation-run44-5492`) for the go-unix-utils project. This is an automated code generation pipeline task. The task description states: \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44. This issue will be closed automatically when measure completes.\" However, the task prompt does NOT contain explicit sections for \"Requirements\", \"Files to Create/Modify\", \"Acceptance Criteria\", or \"Design Decisions\" — meaning the actual work items were not specified. The user then critically instructed me to stop all tool usage and produce a text-only summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **go-unix-utils**: Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing\n   - **cobbler-scaffold pipeline**: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation) workflow\n   - **Differential testing**: `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` compares Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binaries\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **Generation run 44**: Current generation run, tracked on branch `generation-run44`\n   - **SRD-driven development**: Software Requirements Documents drive code generation\n   - **Requirement states**: Many SRDs (srd004-ts through srd114-vidir) have requirements in \"ready\" status awaiting implementation\n   - **Execution constitution**: Strict rules including no git commands, no scope creep, 40-line function limit, copyright headers, write-all-then-build strategy\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** - Differential testing harness; 